The plaint shall contain the following particulars:-
(a) the name of the Court in which the suit is brought;
(b) the name, age, description, place of residence and place of business, if any, of the plaintiff;
(c) the name, age, description, place of residence and the place of business, if any, of the defendant, so far as can be
ascertained by the plaintiff;
(d) where the plaintiff or the defendant is a minor or a person of unsound mind, a statement to that effect and in the case
of a minor, his age to the best of the knowledge and belief of the person verifying the plaint:
Provided that, where, owing to the large number of defendants or any other sufficient cause, it is not practicable to
ascertain with reasonable accuracy the age of the minor defendants, it may be stated that the age of the minor
defendants is not known;
(e) the facts constituting the cause of action and when it arose;
(f) the facts showing that the Court has jurisdiction;
(g) the relief which the plaintiff claims;
(h) where the plaintiff has allowed a set-off or relinquished a portion of the claim, the amount so allowed or relinquished;
and
(i) a statement of the value of the subject-matter of the suit for the purposes of jurisdiction and of Court-fees, so far as
the case admits."-(R.O.C. No. 2526/1959, dated 9-2-1967).
