pass any order relating to the monitoring of recording the evidence by a commission or any other authority;
(q)
order any party to file and exchange a costs budget;
(r)
issue directions or pass any order for the purpose of managing the case and furthering the overriding objective of
ensuring the efficient disposal of the suit.
(2)
When the Court passes an order in exercise of its powers under this Order, it may?
(a)
make it subject to conditions, including a condition to pay a sum of money into Court; and
(b)
specify the consequence of failure to comply with the order or a condition.
(3)
While fixing the date for a Case Management Hearing, the Court may direct that the parties also be present for such
Case Management Hearing, if it is of the view that there is a possibility of settlement between the parties.
